# site keys are public by design — Google requires them to be embedded in the HTML of
# every page that renders the widget, so this exact string is already served to every
# visitor of https://www.refactored.ai/contact-us/. The half that must stay private is
# the reCAPTCHA SECRET key, which lives server-side and is not in this capture.
#
# WHY A FINGERPRINT RATHER THAN AN INLINE `gitleaks:allow`: this file is a byte-faithful
# point-in-time capture of a live page. Editing it to insert a scanner directive would
# change bytes the capture exists to preserve, break the sizes recorded in
# manifest.json, and make a future re-capture diff as though the page had changed. The
# capture must not be edited, so the exception belongs here.
#
# NOTE: line-anchored, and that is correct. Re-running capture.js after the site changes
# will move or remove this line, the finding returns, and it gets re-reviewed rather than
# silently inheriting an old exemption.
